BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Bonnie Jean Alexander
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260714
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTSTAMP:20260801T164623Z
UID:rhodesobit-2026-07-14-bonnie-jean-alexander-2026-07-14-allday@linn-cou
 nty-scraper.local
DESCRIPTION:Bonnie Jean\, age 96\, of Linneus\, passed away on Tuesday\, J
 uly 14\, 2026\, at McLarney Manor in Brookfield\, MO.\n Bonnie Jean was bo
 rn on March 1\, 1930\, in Laclede\, MO to the late Lorenzo Owen and Conna 
 Maud (Massey) Dowell. She attended and graduated from school in Laclede\, 
 MO. On May 8\, 1949\, she married James Dewayne Alexander at the Laclede M
 ethodist Church in Laclede\, MO. After graduation Bonnie worked as a hospi
 tal receptionist at Woodland Hospital in Moberly\, MO. She later worked fo
 r 29 years at the Agricultural Stabilization and Conservation Service (ASC
 S) office in Brookfield\, MO.\n Bonnie was a member of the Linneus United 
 Methodist Church where she was a lead vocalist and choir member for many y
 ears. Bonnie and James were very active with the church’s card club\, an
 d created fond memories at their New Years Eve parties. She was a member o
 f the Order of Eastern Star for over 75 years. She also served on the Linn
  County 4H Fair Board and held the office of Secretary.\n Bonnie’s great
 est joy was her...\n\nFull obituary and service details: https://www.rhode
 sfh.com/obituaries/bonnie-alexander-3/
LOCATION:Linneus\, MO
